  "_configurations": "The 3D data-side sweep: stall signal --mlp_data_bound {0 fu_wait, 1 no_issue} x scope --mlp_data_scope {0 rob_head, 1 all_loads} x threshold --mlp_data_bound_min {4, 8, 16, 32}, 16 arms, each with --mlc_cache_repl_policy 9, the cheaper-hardware countdown boost (--mlp_boost_countdown 1, in place of --mlp_boost_in_fills 1), and the recommended lambdas (--mlp_lin_data_lambda 16 --mlp_lin_instr_lambda 64). mlp_lin_data_thresh is left at its default 0 (ratio gate off) so mlp_data_bound/mlp_data_scope/mlp_data_bound_min alone decide marking. mlp_instr_mark/mlp_instr_starve/mlp_instr_starve_min are left at their REPL_MLP defaults (2, 2, 1) on these 16 arms since they are data-side only.\nPlus a separate instruction-side sweep (not crossed with the above): --mlp_instr_starve {1 backend_starved, 2 backend_starved_and_rob_head_not_load, 3 issue_queue_empty} x --mlp_instr_starve_min {1, 4, 8}, 9 arms, each on top of the same --mlc_cache_repl_policy 9 --mlp_boost_countdown 1 --mlp_lin_data_lambda 16 --mlp_lin_instr_lambda 64, with mlp_data_bound/mlp_data_scope/mlp_data_bound_min left at their REPL_MLP defaults (1 no_issue, 0 rob_head, 16).\nbaseline is plain L2 LRU for reference.",
